{{Short description|Football tournament group stage}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=June 2018}}
Group 1 was one of six groups of national teams competing in the group stage of the [[1982 FIFA World Cup]]. Play began on 14 June and ended on 23 June 1982.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/82full.html |title=World Cup 1982 finals |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref> The group consisted of four teams: Seeded team [[Poland national football team|Poland]], two-time World Cup winners [[Italy national football team|Italy]], [[Peru national football team|Peru]] and World Cup debutants [[Cameroon national football team|Cameroon]].

Poland won the group, having achieved the only victory among the six fixtures in the group, and advanced to the second round. Italy also advanced, ahead of Cameroon, as Italy had scored the greater number of goals. Cameroon therefore exited the tournament undefeated.

Italy went on to win the tournament, and as of 2026 is the last team who failed to win their group to later win the tournament.

